WEBVTT

00:00.750 --> 00:02.930
<i>Previously on Captain Tsubasa.</i>

00:02.930 --> 00:09.820
<i>In a one-to-eleven handicapped match, Tsubasa skillfully controlled the ball and toyed with the adversary team. </i>

00:09.820 --> 00:16.260
<i>And then, thanks to Robert Hongo's cross, former forward of the Brazilian national team who suddenly appeared,</i>

00:16.260 --> 00:20.500
<i>Tsubasa scored a goal and won a splendid victory over Wakabayashi.</i>

00:20.500 --> 00:21.500
<i>I lost!</i>

00:21.500 --> 00:24.790
I lost to that squirt!<i></i>

00:24.790 --> 00:26.080
A match.

00:26.080 --> 00:27.420
We'll play a match!

00:27.850 --> 00:32.240
<i>They decided to settle their score on another day, in the inter-school tournament.</i>

00:32.240 --> 00:38.440
<i>Then, Roberto who had been watching what was going on, offered to be their coach.</i>

00:38.440 --> 00:44.270
<i>And to prove his abilities, he unleashed an overhead kick.</i>

00:45.650 --> 00:46.690
Okay!

00:46.690 --> 00:51.970
<i>He just saw my move, and is trying to copy it right away.</i>

00:51.970 --> 00:56.950
<i>He's the kind who's got a thirst for assimilating all techniques he sees.</i>

00:56.950 --> 00:58.580
Go!

00:59.450 --> 01:04.240
<i>At the end of the practice, Tsubasa managed to perform an overhead kick. </i>

01:04.240 --> 01:09.900
<i>And together with his new friends, he was looking forward to his showdown with Wakabayashi.</i>

01:13.040 --> 01:14.190
<b>Sign: <b>TSUBASA</b></b>

01:26.240 --> 01:27.720
Overhead kick!

01:27.720 --> 01:28.480
Tsubasa…

01:31.870 --> 01:36.300
Huh? What happened, mom? Why are you covered in a blanket?

01:39.130 --> 01:41.990
I wonder why.

01:54.090 --> 01:59.680
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:54.090 --> 01:59.680
<i>koronde toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:59.680 --> 02:04.350
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:59.680 --> 02:04.350
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

02:05.600 --> 02:10.270
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

02:05.600 --> 02:10.270
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

02:11.150 --> 02:18.860
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

02:11.150 --> 02:18.860
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

02:18.860 --> 02:24.620
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

02:18.860 --> 02:24.620
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

02:24.620 --> 02:33.380
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

02:24.620 --> 02:33.380
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

02:33.380 --> 02:38.930
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

02:33.380 --> 02:38.930
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

02:38.930 --> 02:44.850
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

02:38.930 --> 02:44.850
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:44.850 --> 02:46.520
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:46.520 --> 02:53.730
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:46.520 --> 02:53.730
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:53.730 --> 02:56.730
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Go, our kicks!</i>

02:53.730 --> 02:56.730
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kick o</i>

02:56.730 --> 03:01.160
<i>Leap out into a huge TV</i>

02:56.730 --> 03:01.160
<i>tobidasô dodekai TV</i>

03:12.450 --> 03:16.530
<b>EPISODE 3: A NEW BEGINNING FOR THE NANKATSU FOOTBALL CLUB</b>

03:15.850 --> 03:20.140
If you keep on oversleeping so much, it'll become a bad habit.

03:20.140 --> 03:21.950
That’s not true.

03:24.800 --> 03:29.390
Go and wash your face. Your spring break’s ending today.

03:29.860 --> 03:31.430
You’ll be going to school from tomorrow on.

03:32.430 --> 03:33.900
Oh right, school.

03:33.900 --> 03:35.950
How did it go, Mom?

03:35.950 --> 03:39.440
Well, the procedures were quite exhausting...

03:39.900 --> 03:45.040
Since you suddenly wanted to attend Nankatsu Elementary instead of Shuutetsu Elementary.

03:46.130 --> 03:48.450
It's not right unless it’s Nankatsu Elementary.

03:48.450 --> 03:51.660
<i>I'll take your challenge during the inter-school tournament!</i>

03:51.660 --> 03:57.550
<i>But with you on the team I'm sure we can put up a good show!</i>

03:57.550 --> 03:59.050
<i>I made a promise, after all.</i>

03:59.840 --> 04:01.020
Mom!

04:01.020 --> 04:01.840
Yes?

04:02.350 --> 04:05.370
I’m really glad that we moved to this town.

04:05.370 --> 04:10.890
Is that so? Actually, there’s someone I want to introduce to you, Tsubasa.

04:11.850 --> 04:13.270
You can come in.

04:17.480 --> 04:19.150
Roberto Hongo!

04:19.150 --> 04:20.820
Hey there! ‘Good morning!

04:20.820 --> 04:23.680
Why? Wha-- How? HOW?!

04:23.680 --> 04:25.320
Here you are, Tsubasa.

04:25.320 --> 04:26.900
It’s from your father.

04:28.540 --> 04:30.330
Roberto brought it with him.

04:30.330 --> 04:32.050
It's from my dad?

04:36.190 --> 04:37.260
<i>“Dear Tsubasa,</i>

04:38.010 --> 04:46.470
<i>Mr. Roberto Hongo is an excellent professional football player who played as a forward on the Brazilian national team.</i>

04:46.470 --> 04:50.630
<i>Due to circumstances, he has decided to temporarily live in Japan.</i>

04:51.350 --> 04:54.350
<i>I then decided he'd be living at our home.</i>

04:55.490 --> 05:00.990
<i>Tsubasa, I’ve already talked to Mr. Roberto about you. </i>

05:00.990 --> 05:04.910
<i>Learn football from the best to your heart’s content while you can. </i>

05:06.180 --> 05:08.450
<i>I'll be returning home soon.”</i>

05:08.450 --> 05:13.660
This is great! Roberto Hongo will be living with us. It’s great!

05:14.400 --> 05:15.040
Hey.

05:15.040 --> 05:17.060
Since when have you been here?

05:22.030 --> 05:24.830
Your mother mistook me for a thief!

05:24.830 --> 05:25.940
Really?

05:25.940 --> 05:28.340
She threw water over me out of nowhere!

05:28.340 --> 05:31.420
Well, he arrived at 2 in the morning!

05:31.420 --> 05:32.600
At two?!

05:32.600 --> 05:36.600
You should've shown me the letter right away, Roberto.

05:36.600 --> 05:37.430
Really!

05:38.110 --> 05:39.110
Sorry 'bout that.

05:40.570 --> 05:42.240
Are you practicing this afternoon?

05:42.240 --> 05:43.280
Yeah!

05:43.280 --> 05:46.610
Ishizaki will introduce me to the football team today.

05:46.610 --> 05:48.110
I see.

05:48.110 --> 05:51.580
All right! Expect a present from me at that time!

05:51.580 --> 05:53.660
Huh, a present?

05:57.110 --> 05:59.580
It's impossible that Wakabayashi could have lost.

05:59.580 --> 06:01.600
It's unimaginable.

06:01.600 --> 06:05.930
There's no way all of the Shuutetsu team could have lost against one player, is there?

06:05.930 --> 06:08.720
He was up against the B team, but they're still part of the national winning team!

06:08.720 --> 06:10.300
He really did!

06:10.930 --> 06:13.430
He's a totally amazing player!

06:13.430 --> 06:16.000
He's dribbling anywhere he goes!

06:16.000 --> 06:19.030
Could you be talking about him?

06:25.260 --> 06:28.110
Over here, Tsubasa!

06:28.110 --> 06:29.030
Ishizaki!

06:30.780 --> 06:33.330
We were waiting for you, Tsubasa!

06:35.840 --> 06:36.580
There!

06:43.400 --> 06:44.730
Well played!

06:44.730 --> 06:45.770
Ishizaki!

06:45.770 --> 06:46.590
Huh?

06:46.590 --> 06:47.470
Here!

06:47.470 --> 06:49.230
It's mine!

06:49.230 --> 06:49.840
Oops!

06:53.220 --> 06:54.810
Is everything okay?

06:55.790 --> 06:57.870
Don't worry, don't worry!

06:57.870 --> 06:59.730
Huh? Where's Roberto?

06:59.730 --> 07:01.190
He's got something to do.

07:02.700 --> 07:04.440
That's everyone from the football club, right?

07:07.390 --> 07:10.610
They might look like they're good, but actually they're not!

07:11.240 --> 07:14.140
You're not one to talk, Ishizaki!

07:14.140 --> 07:16.100
Your control just now sucked big time!

07:16.100 --> 07:18.620
So what?! Listen, guys!

07:18.620 --> 07:23.500
He's the one who got our football field back; Oozora Tsubasa!

07:23.500 --> 07:24.630
Nice to meet you!

07:24.630 --> 07:26.010
Nice to meet you.

07:26.010 --> 07:29.340
Thank you so much for getting back our field.

07:29.340 --> 07:33.370
I would've liked seeing that Wakabayashi take that goal.

07:33.370 --> 07:35.900
I would have liked that, too!

07:35.900 --> 07:36.790
By the way,

07:37.820 --> 07:41.440
you're joining our team, aren't you?

07:43.830 --> 07:45.350
I am!

07:45.350 --> 07:49.490
I've been transferred to Nankatsu. We'll be playing football together!

07:51.490 --> 07:52.500
Yes!

07:52.500 --> 07:54.340
You're incredibly good at football!

07:54.340 --> 07:56.590
Your shot just now really impressed me!

07:56.590 --> 07:58.590
I told you, didn't I? Didn't I?

07:58.590 --> 08:02.940
What's more, a former Brazilian football player will be coaching us!

08:03.540 --> 08:05.000
Isn't that totally awesome?!

08:05.000 --> 08:08.250
Let the practice of the new Nankatsu team start!

08:08.250 --> 08:10.010
Yeah!

08:14.600 --> 08:16.070
Genzou.<i></i>

08:16.070 --> 08:18.430
<i>How is your injury feeling?</i>

08:18.430 --> 08:21.050
<i>You're supposed to be resting today.</i>

08:23.000 --> 08:25.020
<i>I lost</i>

08:25.760 --> 08:27.290
<i>against Oozora Tsubasa.</i>

08:30.240 --> 08:36.950
<i>Maybe the fact that I didn't let in any goals during the national tournament made me big headed.</i>

08:37.430 --> 08:38.910
<i>Don't worry about it.</i>

08:38.910 --> 08:40.720
<i>That's impossible!</i>

08:42.310 --> 08:44.940
<i>If I can't stop his shots,</i>

08:44.940 --> 08:47.800
<i>becoming champion last year won't mean a thing.</i>

08:56.670 --> 09:00.060
Let's start by running. And after that, do passes by pairs.

09:00.060 --> 09:01.770
Let's get started!

09:07.730 --> 09:10.650
Tsubasa, want to pair up with me for the passes?

09:10.650 --> 09:11.330
Sure!

09:28.500 --> 09:29.860
Say, Tsubasa...

09:30.850 --> 09:34.840
I checked out something about you that intrigued me since yesterday.

09:34.840 --> 09:37.050
You're incredibly good at football,

09:37.050 --> 09:40.390
but you've never been in the national football tournament.

09:40.390 --> 09:43.030
Didn't your old school have a football club?

09:44.250 --> 09:46.140
It had, but...

09:46.640 --> 09:48.550
It wasn't too good.

09:48.550 --> 09:50.150
Even with you there?

09:51.650 --> 09:54.650
Its members didn't love football.

09:54.650 --> 09:57.200
Some of them could only think about shooting.

09:57.720 --> 10:00.840
Or quit because they found the practices too hard.

10:00.840 --> 10:02.870
Those kinds are everywhere.

10:02.870 --> 10:05.140
They all want to be forwards.

10:05.140 --> 10:07.320
But not everyone can score.

10:07.320 --> 10:09.710
And so, they think it's boring.

10:09.710 --> 10:12.890
<i>That's</i> why you practice, right?

10:13.910 --> 10:14.960
In the end,

10:14.960 --> 10:19.150
all of us here love football. Right, guys?

10:19.150 --> 10:20.840
Yeah, you're right about that!

10:20.840 --> 10:22.850
Of course we do!

10:22.850 --> 10:27.460
Or else we wouldn't be taking a spanking from Shuutetsu every year!

10:30.150 --> 10:31.770
Someone's coming.

10:37.870 --> 10:39.490
What do you guys want?!

10:54.600 --> 10:56.050
Yo, Ishizaki.

10:56.050 --> 10:57.530
Urabe!

10:58.220 --> 10:59.480
Who's that team?

10:59.550 --> 11:01.720
The football club of Nishigaoka Elementary School.

11:02.310 --> 11:04.170
It's a school from the neighbouring town.

11:04.170 --> 11:06.740
They are a pretty good team.

11:06.770 --> 11:09.060
As promised, we have come.

11:09.060 --> 11:11.030
What promise are you talking about?

11:11.030 --> 11:13.150
Don't give me that crap!

11:13.150 --> 11:16.470
It was you who wanted to have a practice match with us!

11:16.470 --> 11:17.580
What...?

11:17.580 --> 11:18.780
Hey!

11:20.110 --> 11:21.070
Roberto!

11:21.460 --> 11:24.030
It was my idea!

11:24.030 --> 11:27.160
You are finally here, coach!
You are late!

11:28.450 --> 11:30.570
What? Is that Roberto Hongo?

11:30.570 --> 11:31.230
Yeah.

11:31.790 --> 11:33.810
But he's drinking...

11:33.810 --> 11:35.590
Is that really him?

11:35.590 --> 11:37.870
Yeah, that's him!
Don't you recognize him?

11:37.870 --> 11:41.820
He's the incredible player on the news that's being talked about who's got Japanese origins!

11:41.820 --> 11:43.090
Is that so?

11:43.090 --> 11:47.100
Will he be alright? He's drinking alcohol even though it's only afternoon.

11:47.100 --> 11:49.160
He's not just a drunkard!

11:49.160 --> 11:51.020
He's really great!

11:51.700 --> 11:54.810
Is this the present you've been talking about this morning?

11:54.810 --> 11:55.440
That's right!

11:55.440 --> 11:57.910
What a disgusting team!

11:57.910 --> 11:59.000
What did you say?

11:59.000 --> 12:01.600
Your coach is an alcoholic.

12:01.600 --> 12:02.850
Roberto is...

12:08.160 --> 12:13.580
Even though he looks different from when he used to play, he's the real deal.

12:13.580 --> 12:14.710
Are you serious?

12:14.710 --> 12:18.490
He was in the spotlight for a while,
but he suddenly disappeared.

12:18.490 --> 12:20.200
I'm counting on you!

12:21.220 --> 12:22.930
Is it because of the alcohol?

12:22.930 --> 12:24.050
It might be.

12:25.760 --> 12:27.920
You sure have picked up a weird coach!

12:27.920 --> 12:28.640
Huh?

12:28.640 --> 12:33.650
No wonder you lost 30 to 0 when you played against Shuutetsu!

12:34.850 --> 12:36.690
30 to 0?

12:38.980 --> 12:42.600
If we want to take Shuutetsu down,

12:42.600 --> 12:45.550
we need to at least win as much.

12:46.270 --> 12:47.240
Well said!

12:47.240 --> 12:50.830
That bastard! He sure doesn't hold back his words!

12:50.830 --> 12:53.060
30 to 0? Is he serious?

12:53.060 --> 12:54.780
Well... Yeah...

12:54.780 --> 12:58.810
Tsubasa! I'm counting on you to shut them up!

12:58.810 --> 12:59.500
Sure!

12:59.930 --> 13:01.570
Well, let's begin!

13:01.570 --> 13:03.740
It'll get dark if we don't hurry up!

13:03.740 --> 13:06.260
What are you talking about! It's still noon, you fool!

13:16.020 --> 13:19.400
Well, maybe I should do something coach-like.

13:19.400 --> 13:22.150
Then start with that booze!

13:22.150 --> 13:24.340
Once you're here, it's forbidden!

13:25.690 --> 13:26.660
I see...

13:27.770 --> 13:31.350
You are supposed to throw it in the trash!

13:31.350 --> 13:34.350
But I just bought it, wouldn't it be a waste?

13:35.670 --> 13:37.900
He's so uncool when he's not on the field!

13:37.900 --> 13:39.170
Calm down, Ryo!

13:39.170 --> 13:42.420
By the way, who will be your captain, guys?

13:42.420 --> 13:45.410
Well, you could say that I am the captain.

13:45.410 --> 13:46.290
Oh, are you?

13:46.290 --> 13:47.710
We haven't decided yet.

13:47.710 --> 13:51.100
What are you talking about?
I've always been the captain!

13:51.100 --> 13:55.550
Then Ishizaki, make some noise and guide the others in the field.

13:55.550 --> 13:57.100
Okay, got it!

13:57.100 --> 13:58.960
That's what you always do.

13:58.960 --> 14:00.810
Even though you only yell "run, run"...

14:00.810 --> 14:02.070
That's enough!

14:02.070 --> 14:03.780
It's fine.

14:03.780 --> 14:05.070
The sound of the captain

14:05.070 --> 14:06.820
motivates everyone.

14:06.820 --> 14:07.760
Yeah!

14:07.760 --> 14:10.330
Roberto, don't we have any other tactics?

14:10.330 --> 14:12.830
Hmm, good question...

14:14.080 --> 14:14.920
Not really.

14:14.920 --> 14:15.750
What?!

14:16.250 --> 14:19.100
I want to start by seeing at what level each one of you are at.

14:19.100 --> 14:21.250
A match is perfect for that.

14:22.070 --> 14:25.110
I'll judge what you can do in your position.

14:25.110 --> 14:27.610
Give it all you've got.

14:27.610 --> 14:29.010
Okay!

14:30.570 --> 14:31.510
Tsubasa!

14:31.510 --> 14:33.410
Yes, Roberto?

14:33.410 --> 14:34.470
Don't forget.

14:35.080 --> 14:36.730
The ball is your friend.

14:40.180 --> 14:42.440
The ball is waiting for you

14:42.440 --> 14:44.280
to play with it.

14:47.050 --> 14:48.990
Okay, do it guys!

14:49.450 --> 14:50.820
Yes, coach!

15:04.380 --> 15:06.840
Let's have a good game, Mr. Referee.

15:06.840 --> 15:08.350
Thanks.

15:14.720 --> 15:19.730
The practice match between
Nishigaoka and Nankatsu is about to begin!

15:20.170 --> 15:21.480
There's twenty minutes per half!

15:21.480 --> 15:24.230
Nishigaoka will kick-off!

15:31.000 --> 15:34.660
<i>Who's that? I don't remember having seen him at Nankatsu.</i>

15:35.110 --> 15:38.790
<i>Whatever, he won't make a difference against us anyway.</i>

15:39.250 --> 15:43.540
All right, let's go get the first of 30 goals, guys!

15:43.540 --> 15:44.540
Yeah!

15:44.540 --> 15:46.130
He's making fun of us!

15:48.840 --> 15:49.820
What?

15:51.580 --> 15:52.720
Nice pass!

15:53.530 --> 15:55.600
Is something the matter?

16:00.070 --> 16:02.020
Let's stop them, guys!

16:12.460 --> 16:13.620
Urabe!

16:18.790 --> 16:20.330
What a lousy tackle!

16:20.770 --> 16:26.420
That's not how you stop the captain of Nishigaoka Urabe Hanji's dribbling!

16:29.400 --> 16:30.550
What?

16:31.030 --> 16:31.550
Huh?

16:31.550 --> 16:32.050
No way!

16:32.050 --> 16:33.800
Well done, Tsubasa!

16:33.800 --> 16:35.140
Awesome!

16:37.640 --> 16:39.270
Attack!

16:41.980 --> 16:44.730
Tsubasa, what are you doing?

16:44.730 --> 16:46.980
You're going towards <i>our</i> goal!

16:46.980 --> 16:48.680
Tsubasa!

16:56.280 --> 16:57.530
Here I go!

17:04.470 --> 17:05.380
Here's my shot!

17:20.140 --> 17:21.020
It's in!

17:21.020 --> 17:22.140
That's crazy!

17:25.960 --> 17:27.890
Well done, Tsubasa!

17:27.890 --> 17:29.900
I've never seen something like that!

17:29.900 --> 17:32.400
You're such a show-off!

17:33.580 --> 17:35.030
We did it guys!

17:35.030 --> 17:37.760
So good! What a great shot from that distance!

17:37.760 --> 17:39.490
We scored! We did it! We did it!

17:40.470 --> 17:42.810
Who the hell is this guy?

17:42.810 --> 17:43.750
Has there always been

17:44.220 --> 17:46.250
a guy like him at Nankatsu?

17:48.790 --> 17:50.710
Come on guys, let's counter-attack!

17:55.970 --> 18:00.970
<b>Sign: NANKATSU: 2
NISHIGAOKA: 0</b>

18:02.720 --> 18:05.310
We're still only down by two, we can still come back!

18:06.190 --> 18:07.560
You again?!

18:14.530 --> 18:15.780
Huh, me?

18:17.070 --> 18:18.420
Uh, sorry!

18:18.420 --> 18:20.260
What's his name?

18:20.260 --> 18:21.450
It's Iwami.

18:28.260 --> 18:29.290
Bring it on!

18:29.290 --> 18:30.290
Iwami!

18:32.870 --> 18:34.210
Whoa, I did it!

18:34.210 --> 18:37.050
Of course!
Stay calm, and everything will be fine!

18:40.320 --> 18:41.720
Iwami!

18:41.720 --> 18:42.670
Over here!

18:44.430 --> 18:45.930
You can't have it!

18:50.190 --> 18:50.980
What?!

18:52.380 --> 18:53.570
Excellent!

18:54.570 --> 18:57.070
He's free in front of the goal!

18:57.320 --> 18:58.820
Everyone, watch this!

19:04.510 --> 19:05.740
Oh, damn!

19:05.740 --> 19:07.650
That was pretty close, Ishizaki!

19:07.650 --> 19:08.870
That's right!

19:08.870 --> 19:11.200
Guys, let's keep gunning at them!

19:11.200 --> 19:12.740
Just follow my lead!

19:12.740 --> 19:15.450
You mean Tsubasa's, right?

19:16.030 --> 19:18.880
U-Uh... Shut up! No need to be punctilious!

19:33.180 --> 19:34.900
<i>This Oozora Tsubasa</i>

19:34.900 --> 19:36.650
<i>is incredible.</i>

19:38.100 --> 19:40.610
<i>He builds the game by himself.</i>

19:42.120 --> 19:43.410
<i>This team</i>

19:43.880 --> 19:46.280
<i>has never played like this before.</i>

19:47.660 --> 19:50.160
<b>Sign:
<b>NANKATSU : 4
NISHIGAOKA : 2</b></b>

19:50.160 --> 19:53.670
Him! As long as you can mark that player, it will be enough!

19:53.670 --> 19:56.170
Don't mind the other players!

19:57.670 --> 19:59.590
Go all together if you have to.

19:59.590 --> 20:02.850
Just stop Oozora Tsubasa's dribbles!

20:02.850 --> 20:03.680
Gotcha!

20:07.600 --> 20:09.110
I'm not letting you past me!

20:09.110 --> 20:09.600
Come!

20:11.520 --> 20:13.100
Pass the ball, Tsubasa!

20:16.070 --> 20:16.900
What?

20:21.650 --> 20:22.950
Tsubasa!

20:22.950 --> 20:24.120
Ishizaki!

20:28.580 --> 20:29.900
I'm crossing!

20:29.900 --> 20:31.210
Huh, what?

20:31.210 --> 20:32.710
Huh, it's for me?

20:32.710 --> 20:34.350
Make it count, Ishizaki!

20:34.350 --> 20:35.210
Ishizaki!

20:49.140 --> 20:50.270
He scored!

20:50.270 --> 20:51.140
He did it!

20:54.490 --> 20:55.860
I can't believe it...

21:01.520 --> 21:04.160
That hurts!

21:07.830 --> 21:10.840
I-I...

21:10.840 --> 21:12.330
...scored a goal...

21:12.330 --> 21:14.280
I've scored a goal.

21:17.970 --> 21:19.460
End of the match!

21:19.460 --> 21:22.130
<b>Sign:
NANKATSU : 5
NISHIGAOKA : 2</b>

21:22.130 --> 21:24.380
We won!

21:24.380 --> 21:27.340
We did it! We won!

21:27.340 --> 21:29.390
I'm so happy! {or I'm so happy}

21:29.860 --> 21:33.140
Tsubasa!
It's all thanks to you!

21:33.140 --> 21:36.580
You're the one who scored the last goal, Ishizaki!

21:36.580 --> 21:37.400
Besides,

21:37.400 --> 21:39.430
everyone did their best!

21:45.830 --> 21:48.000
We've lost to Nankatsu...

21:49.200 --> 21:50.910
Oozora Tsubasa!

21:51.380 --> 21:53.510
It's all your fault!

21:56.680 --> 22:00.550
<i>Tsubasa! I can not wait to challenge you at the inter-school tournament!</i>

22:03.030 --> 22:05.750
<i>I've understood each one of your's habits.</i>

22:06.390 --> 22:07.960
<i>Now I know what to do.</i>

22:09.120 --> 22:10.830
<i>But above all,</i>

22:10.830 --> 22:13.060
<i>you'll all have to become friends</i>

22:14.040 --> 22:15.750
<i>with the ball.</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.730
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.730
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.730 --> 23:02.860
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.730 --> 23:02.860
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:02.860 --> 23:08.950
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:02.860 --> 23:08.950
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:08.950 --> 23:15.040
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:08.950 --> 23:15.040
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.040 --> 23:21.080
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.550 --> 23:33.260
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.550 --> 23:33.260
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.260 --> 23:39.140
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:45.690
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:45.690
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.570 --> 23:59.190
<b>COMING UP, EPISODE 4:
TSUBASA AND ROBERTO</b>
